 :root-cause
 "The cursor-rebase scaling fixture compared successful single-chunk decisions with multi-chunk tail decisions. Multi-chunk success necessarily includes intermediate generated :restarted chunk results, so the endpoint ratio mixed two operation shapes instead of measuring one asymptotic domain. Running the JVM gate after a ClojureScript compiler build made the smallest single-chunk allocation unusually low and exposed the invalid comparison as a deterministic false positive."
 :fix
 "Measure JVM and JavaScript scaling over a fourfold size range wholly within each runtime's multi-chunk domain, fail the gate when a supplied fixture violates that domain, restart a fresh heap-bounded JVM before the JVM cursor gate, and print the complete observation before throwing. Preserve every latency, allocation, heap-delta, logical-work, and one-million-identity ceiling."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.characterization-fixture-test/quantitative-performance-gates-are-well-formed-test"
  "eacl.formal.cursor-rebase-benchmark/run-gate!"
  ".github/workflows/formal.yml/Restart heap-bounded nREPL for cursor resource gate"
  "formal/verification/performance-gates.edn"]}
